# .clinerules for Zip-OR-Folder-to-Context Tool Project

## Project Goal & Scope
- Objective: Create a client-side only web tool (HTML/CSS/JS) to read EITHER a ZIP file OR a user-selected Folder, concatenate file contents (with paths), and display the result for LLM context.
- CRITICAL: No backend code. All processing must happen in the browser.
- Output: Single HTML file containing embedded CSS and JS, or clearly separated blocks.

## Technology Stack & Libraries
- Frontend: HTML5 (using `webkitdirectory` for folder input), CSS3, Modern JavaScript (ES6+ including async/await, FileReader API).
- REQUIRED Library: JSZip for client-side ZIP decompression.
- NO Server-Side: Do not include any backend code or dependencies.

## Core Functionality Requirements
- Input Handling: Must support both ZIP file input (`accept=".zip"`) AND Folder input (`webkitdirectory`). Handle logic based on which input was used.
- ZIP Processing: Use JSZip library correctly.
- Folder Processing: Iterate through `FileList`, use `file.webkitRelativePath` for paths. Use `FileReader` to read file content.
- Text vs. Binary Handling:
    - Implement logic to distinguish text files from binary files.
    - Include a single shared checkbox (`id="includeBinary"`) for non-text files.
    - Base64 encode binary files if checkbox is checked; skip if unchecked.
- Output Concatenation:
    - Strictly follow the format:
      ```
      File: [Full Path]
      -----------------
      [Content or Base64 String]
      -----------------

      ```
    - Ensure correct relative path is used for both ZIP and Folder inputs.

## User Interface (UI) Elements & Behavior
- Required Elements: Separate inputs/buttons for ZIP vs Folder, "Include non-text files" checkbox, read-only output textarea, "Copy to Clipboard" button, status/error message area.
- Error Handling: Display user-friendly messages for errors (invalid zip, read errors).
- Status Updates: Provide feedback like "Processing...", "Done!".